<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2853" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαιρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ill-timed,
			unseasonable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς ἄκαιρα πονεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					919
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἄκαιρα λέγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1036
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. κένωσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>VM</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προθυμία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.65
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλευθερία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					569c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπαινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					24c
				</span></i>
			e; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥᾳθυμία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.46
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέλως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					<u>Mon.</u>
					88
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					808
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				624
			</span></i> (both lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Acut.</u>
				17
			</span></i>, al.: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-οτέρως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					1.19
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαιρ᾽ ἀπώλλυτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					1081
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>importunate, troublesome</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. καὶ λάλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.62
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.
			inf., <i>ill-suited</i> to do a thing, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.Mag.</u>
				7.6
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκαιρον, τό,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρσίνη ἀγρία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.144
			</span></i>.</div>
